---
// The overview index idiom, device 4 of 8: the list the entries sit in.
// See IndexHeader.astro for the family rationale.
//
// Four utilities and no children of its own, which is precisely why it is a
// component: `list-none m-0 p-0 mbs-10` restated at both indexes is two places
// for the English and Hebrew lists to start disagreeing about their top
// margin, and a Hebrew index that sat 8px higher is the kind of second-class
// detail specs/pages/translations-index.md §5 exists to forbid.
//
// `m-0` before `mbs-10` is not a coincidence of writing order — Tailwind sorts
// the margin shorthand ahead of the block-start longhand, so the 40px survives
// the reset. Verified against the emitted CSS in 4.3.3 rather than assumed;
// the reverse order would have zeroed it silently. Same for `p-0`.
---

<ul class="list-none m-0 p-0 mbs-10"><slot /></ul>
